Third-party software
--------------------

THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES lists every Python and Node package this product is built
from, with its licence, as declared by the package. It is generated from the
lockfiles at release time (scripts/release/release_tool.py third-party-licenses).
Operating-system packages inside the container images are listed in each
image's CycloneDX SBOM (autosecops-<version>-image-<component>-<arch>.cdx.json,
attached to every release and to the image itself as an attestation).

The base images are Debian (python:3.12-slim, node:22-bookworm-slim) and
contain GPL and LGPL licensed programs and libraries. The corresponding source
code is available from Debian (https://sources.debian.org/) for the package
versions the image SBOMs list; SingularityRD will also provide it on request
through the contact in SECURITY.md for three years from the release.

Components run next to AutoSecOps and shipped unmodified (container images, in
the air-gap bundle and pulled by Compose, Helm and the desktop app):

  Redis 7.2.16 (redis:7.2.16-alpine)       BSD-3-Clause
  PostgreSQL 16 (postgres:16-alpine)        PostgreSQL License
  Bifrost (maximhq/bifrost)                 Apache-2.0
  Ollama (ollama/ollama)                    MIT
  curl (curlimages/curl)                    curl License

Redis is pinned to 7.2.x on purpose: Redis 7.4 and later are not under an open
source licence (RSALv2 / SSPLv1).


