AutoSecOps does not modify the model.


Detection rule corpora
----------------------

The air-gap bundle can include snapshots of these community rule repositories
(rules/<clone>.tar.gz). They are unmodified copies, each under its own licence,
and each snapshot is shipped with that repository's own licence file next to it
(rules/<clone>.LICENSE). That file prevails over this summary.

  Sigma (SigmaHQ/sigma)                                   Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1
  Elastic detection-rules (elastic/detection-rules)       Elastic License 2.0
  Splunk ESCU (splunk/security_content)                   Apache-2.0
  KQL queries (Bert-JanP/Hunting-Queries-Detection-Rules) BSD-3-Clause

The DRL 1.1 asks that rule authors be credited when rules are used or shared;
the author field of each Sigma rule is kept. The Elastic License 2.0 does not
allow providing the rules to third parties as a hosted or managed service.
